</figure>
<div id="S5.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Poison Ratio.</span> Table <a href="#S5.T5" title="TABLE V ‣ V-H Hyperparameter analysis ‣ V Evaluation ‣ 𝖤𝗆𝖻𝖳𝗋𝖺𝖼𝗄𝖾𝗋: Traceable Black-box Watermarking for Federated Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">V</span></a> presents the impact of varying the poison ratio in the watermark training set. The results indicate that increasing the proportion of poisoned samples leads to a rapid improvement in VR performance. In particular, a poison ratio as low as 5% is sufficient for <math id="S5.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{EmbTracker}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖤𝗆𝖻𝖳𝗋𝖺𝖼𝗄𝖾𝗋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{EmbTracker}</annotation></semantics></math> to achieve VR that exceeds 95% on the NQ dataset, demonstrating the efficiency and effectiveness of the proposed watermarking scheme with minimal data modification.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE VI: </span>Impact of watermark training epochs on VR. Different epochs all bring high VRs exceeding 95%.</figcaption>
